course: dictionary
lesson: 8324
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The best way to find the right one is to read the words around it, which is its context. «A fishing rod is a long pole with a line, used to catch fish.» Here rod means a pole, because the fishing and the line are clues.
explain: Now read this: «A lightning rod gives that spark an easy metal path down into the earth.» Nobody is fishing here, so the fishing meaning does not fit. A lightning rod is a metal stick that protects a building. Always ask: does my meaning still make sense in this sentence?
explain: Some meanings are old or special. Long ago, a rod was a unit of length, about 5 metres. In the saying «rule with a rod of iron», rod means ruling very strictly. When a word has many meanings, check the clues, then test each meaning in the sentence.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Rod» means a long thin straight stick of wood, metal or plastic.
fact: «Fishing rod» means a long pole with a line, used to catch fish.
fact: A rod is an old unit of length, about 5 metres, or 5½ yards.
fact: Rods are also cells in the eye that help you see in dim light.
exercise: «A lightning rod gives that spark an easy metal path down into the earth.» What is a lightning rod? | An old unit of length | A pole used to catch fish | A cell in the eye that sees in dim light | *A metal stick that protects a building from lightning
exercise: Maya reads «a fishing rod» and asks what rod means there. What is the answer? | A kind of tree | *A long pole with a line, used to catch fish | A cell in the eye | A unit of length about 5 metres
exercise: «The pencil is a rod of baked graphite and clay.» What does rod mean in this sentence? | *A long thin straight stick | An old unit of length | A fishing pole | A cell in the eye
test: Which meaning fits «the curtain rod snapped in the wind»? | A cell in the eye | A unit of length of about 5 metres | *A long thin straight stick
test: «He was ruled with a rod of iron.» What does this saying suggest? | Ruled very quickly | Ruled very politely | *Ruled very strictly
exam: Read «Rods help you see in dim light.» Which meaning of rod fits best? | An old unit of length | A fishing pole | *A cell in the eye | A long thin straight stick
